    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d32-a2">

                <pb facs="0152" n="44" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg44"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2 in No.
                    485—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Senhor Pereira to Mr.
                            Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Rio
                                de Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1893-08-02"><hi rendition="#italic">August 2,
                        1893</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>I have before me the note which Mr. E. H. Conger, envoy extraordinary and
                    minister plenipotentiary of the United States of America, addressed me on the
                    31st ultimo, thanking me for the notice of the reestablishment of cipher
                    telegraphic communications between his country, this capital, and the States of
                    the North.</p>
                <p>As to the request which the Mr. Minister formulates in respect to Santos, I
                    regret to say to him it is not possible, however, to extend to that city the
                    measure mentioned.</p>
                <p>I improve the opportunity to have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jo. Filippe
                    Pereira.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
